.TH MAGUS 1 "" "magus" "magus Manual"
.SH NAME
magus \- workspace-aware build orchestrator and content-addressed cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B magus
.RI [ flags ]\ <subcommand>\ [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
magus is a standalone build orchestrator and content\-addressed cache for
multi\-language monorepos, and an evolution of Mage. It provides workspace\-aware
subcommands for building, testing, linting, and inspecting projects without
requiring Mage to be installed.
.PP
magus reads optional configuration from magus.yaml (XDG, workspace root, or
CWD) and MAGUS_* environment variables. All configuration can be overridden
with CLI flags.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
Global flags are accepted by every subcommand and may appear before or
after the subcommand word. Last\-write\-wins, matching kubectl conventions.
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fIpath\fR
Workspace root. Default: walk up from cwd until go.mod is found. Must precede the subcommand.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIpath\fR
Config file path. Default: search for magus.yaml in CWD, workspace root, and $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magus/. Must precede the subcommand.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fIfmt\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fIfmt\fR
Output format: text (default), json, yaml, name, jsonl, or template[=<go\-template>]. Honored by subcommands that emit structured data. A template body renders a Go text/template over the same value \-o json emits (field names are the json keys); a bare \-o template with no body lists that output's fields instead of rendering \- the json keys usable in \-o json and \-o template, with each field's type and doc.
.TP
\fB\-\-concurrency\fR \fIN\fR
Maximum number of concurrent build steps. 0 means use the configured value (or MAGUS_CONCURRENCY, or concurrency_profile, balanced (min(NumCPU,8)) by default).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Increase log verbosity. Repeat for more detail (\-v, \-vv, \-vvv).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.RS
.TP
\fBls\fR
List all discovered projects. See \fBmagus\-ls\fR(1).
.TP
\fBdescribe\fR
Define a magus concept and list its entities. See \fBmagus\-describe\fR(1).
.TP
\fBrun\fR
Run a target for selected projects. See \fBmagus\-run\fR(1).
.TP
\fBx\fR
Reproduce an output ref, or pick project + target. See \fBmagus\-x\fR(1).
.TP
\fBwhere\fR
Print the absolute path of a project. See \fBmagus\-where\fR(1).
.TP
\fBaffected\fR
Run a target for VCS\-diff affected projects. See \fBmagus\-affected\fR(1).
.TP
\fBgraph\fR
The workspace's graphs as objects: deps, export, stats. See \fBmagus\-graph\fR(1).
.TP
\fBquery\fR
Search the knowledge graph, and retrieve a run's output or journal by id. See \fBmagus\-query\fR(1).
.TP
\fBexplain\fR
Show one knowledge\-graph node's context: data, edges, and reach. See \fBmagus\-explain\fR(1).
.TP
\fBpath\fR
Connect two knowledge\-graph nodes: the shortest chain of edges between them. See \fBmagus\-path\fR(1).
.TP
\fBrefs\fR
List where an ingested code symbol is defined and referenced. See \fBmagus\-refs\fR(1).
.TP
\fBwatch\fR
Emit changed file paths to stdout. See \fBmagus\-watch\fR(1).
.TP
\fBevents\fR
Stream workspace events as JSONL for an integration to consume. See \fBmagus\-events\fR(1).
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Inspect concurrency pool and configuration. See \fBmagus\-status\fR(1).
.TP
\fBclean\fR
Remove declared outputs (regenerable, never sources). See \fBmagus\-clean\fR(1).
.TP
\fBshell\fR
Check a command against this workspace's conventions before running it. See \fBmagus\-shell\fR(1).
.TP
\fBvcs\fR
Staging and conflict resolution that knows what is generated. See \fBmagus\-vcs\fR(1).
.TP
\fBqueue\fR
Merge approved changes through a speculative, partitioned merge queue. See \fBmagus\-queue\fR(1).
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Validate the workspace. See \fBmagus\-doctor\fR(1).
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
View or update magus configuration. See \fBmagus\-config\fR(1).
.TP
\fBsession\fR
What magus invocations did and what agents are blocked on: humans read and dispose, hosts write. See \fBmagus\-session\fR(1).
.TP
\fBmemory\fR
Durable cross\-session project memory. See \fBmagus\-memory\fR(1).
.TP
\fBjob\fR
Fork a job, take it, return it with its result, and verify that result. See \fBmagus\-job\fR(1).
.TP
\fBnotes\fR
Human\-authored notes committed to the repository. See \fBmagus\-notes\fR(1).
.TP
\fBdiff\fR
Read the working tree's changes in the order they deserve attention. See \fBmagus\-diff\fR(1).
.TP
\fBserver\fR
Manage the magus server: MCP, the console, APIs and background jobs. See \fBmagus\-server\fR(1).
.TP
\fBbroker\fR
The per\-user process holding this host's capacity and shared services. See \fBmagus\-broker\fR(1).
.TP
\fBmcp\fR
Serve MCP over stdio for the agent host that launched it. See \fBmagus\-mcp\fR(1).
.TP
\fBbuzz\fR
Run a Buzz script. See \fBmagus\-buzz\fR(1).
.TP
\fBcompletion\fR
Print a shell completion script. See \fBmagus\-completion\fR(1).
.TP
\fBman\fR
Install the man pages embedded in this binary. See \fBmagus\-man\fR(1).
.TP
\fBinit\fR
Bootstrap a workspace (magus.yaml + magusfile.buzz + merge driver). See \fBmagus\-init\fR(1).
.TP
\fBspell\fR
Build, publish, pull and list spells as OCI artifacts, and pin them in magus.lock. See \fBmagus\-spell\fR(1).
.TP
\fBagent\fR
Manage skills, harnesses, and agent feedback. See \fBmagus\-agent\fR(1).
.TP
\fBself\fR
Manage the magus binary (update, refresh, registry, install\-shorthand). See \fBmagus\-self\fR(1).
.TP
\fBversion\fR
Print the client and server versions. See \fBmagus\-version\fR(1).
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.RS
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_DIR\fR
Override the default cache location (.magus/ in the workspace root). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.dir\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_WRITE_ENABLED\fR
When false (or 0), replay cache hits but never write new entries, locally or to a remote (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.write.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_REMOTE_WRITE_ENABLED\fR
When false (or 0), write the local cache tier but never the remote tier. Unset, the remote tier is written when the local tier is and a signing key is held. True makes remote writes required: an error without a signing key or with cache.write.enabled false, and a failed remote write fails the step (default: cache.write.enabled). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.remote.write.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_INCLUDE_OS_ENABLED\fR
When true, the host OS keys every cache entry; off by default because a manifest guard already refuses a cross\-platform replay (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.include.os.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_INCLUDE_ARCH_ENABLED\fR
When true, the host architecture keys every cache entry; off by default because a manifest guard already refuses a cross\-platform replay (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.include.arch.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_SIZE_MB\fR
Cache disk usage cap in MB (binary, 1<<20); 0 means unlimited (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.size_mb\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_REMOTE_TRUSTED_KEYS\fR
Comma\-separated base64 Ed25519 public keys a remote artifact must be signed by; required when a remote backend is wired. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.remote.trusted_keys\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_REMOTE_INSECURE\fR
Disable remote\-cache signature verification (accept/produce unsigned artifacts); for trusted single\-repo CI only. Requires cache.remote.insecure_reason (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.remote.insecure\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_REMOTE_INSECURE_REASON\fR
Why this cache runs unverified; required whenever cache.remote.insecure is true. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBcache.remote.insecure_reason\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_SIGNING_KEY\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: the Ed25519 seed that signs remote\-cache writes (see `magus config cache\-key`); env\-only because a signing secret in a committed file is not a secret
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CACHE_TOOL_VERSION\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: how tool versions key the cache: project (per project), workspace (once for the workspace), or off (default: project)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_FORMAT\fR
Output format: pretty, plain, text, or json (default: pretty). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBlog.format\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_LEVEL\fR
Minimum log level: trace, debug, info, warn, error (trace also prints the startup timing table) (default: info). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBlog.level\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_SILENT\fR
When true, the env equivalent of \-s/\-\-silent: suppress progress, bound the failing\-project dump, and surface only lines a target marks as a notice (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBlog.silent\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_STREAM\fR
When true, the env equivalent of \-vv: stream every target's output live instead of withholding a passing target's output (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBlog.stream\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CONCURRENCY\fR
Maximum number of concurrently running per\-project build steps; overrides concurrency_profile when positive (default: concurrency_profile decides). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBconcurrency\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CONCURRENCY_PROFILE\fR
Default build width relative to the machine: conservative (half the cores), balanced (min(cores,8)), or aggressive (every core, and all usable memory minus a 512 MiB floor). Unset is balanced everywhere; CI asks for aggressive explicitly (default: balanced). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBconcurrency_profile\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_BROKER\fR
Whether a run asks the broker for this host's capacity and shared services: required refuses a step when none answers (MGS3022, exit 69), best\-effort runs unarbitrated and says so once, off never starts or contacts one (default: best\-effort). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBbroker\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_HISTORY_PATH\fR
Path to the runtime\-history JSON shared by volatility detection, the CI forecaster, graph timing, and bisect (default: $XDG_STATE_HOME/magus/history/v1.json). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBhistory_path\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_DRY_RUN\fR
When 1 or true, print what would run without executing anything (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBdry_run\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MAX_FAILURES\fR
How many projects may fail before a run stops starting more; 1 is fail\-fast, 0 is unlimited (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmax_failures\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TARGET_TIMEOUT\fR
Duration after which magus cancels any single target, subprocesses included; 0 means no limit (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtarget_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_STALL_TIMEOUT\fR
Abort an invocation that starts, finishes and prints nothing for this long; negative turns the watchdog off (default: 15m). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBstall_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_DEFAULT_CHARMS\fR
Comma\-separated charms applied to every magus run/x by default (e.g. rw); the ci anchor still strips rw, and \-\-no\-default\-charms ignores them for one run. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBdefault_charms\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VCS_ENABLED\fR
Master switch for VCS\-driven affected detection; false makes affected fall back to all projects (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvcs.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VCS_NAME\fR
Pin the active VCS by name (git, hg, sl, jj); empty autodetects from .git/.hg/.sl/.jj. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvcs.name\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VCS_BASE_REF\fR
Default base ref for the active VCS adapter, e.g. origin/main for git. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvcs.base_ref\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VCS_<NAME>_BASE_REF\fR
Per\-VCS base\-ref override, e.g. MAGUS_VCS_GIT_BASE_REF; dynamic pattern, read directly by package vcs
.TP
\fBMAGUS_PROC_SOCKET\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: the proc\-server socket a magus process exports for the magus processes it spawns; unix:// URL or bare path, read directly by the process that adopts it
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CI_MAX_SHARDS\fR
Maximum number of parallel CI shards; \-1 means unlimited (default: 8). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBci.max_shards\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CI_RUNNER_POOL_BUDGET\fR
Cross\-shard concurrency cap at the GHA matrix level; 0 means unlimited (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBci.runner_pool_budget\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CI_RECORD_RUNS\fR
Keep the per\-branch run log (which commit a branch passed or failed at) in the history file (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBci.record_runs\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SHARD\fR
CI matrix shard ID (e.g. "0"); equivalent to magus run \-\-shard; set by .github/actions/magus
.TP
\fBMAGUS_N_SHARDS\fR
Total shard count for this matrix run; equivalent to magus run \-\-n\-shards; set by .github/actions/magus
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_ENABLED\fR
Turn OTLP export on; magus connects to telemetry.endpoint when true (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT\fR
OTLP collector address as host:port (no scheme); required when telemetry is enabled. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.endpoint\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_PROTOCOL\fR
OTLP wire protocol: grpc or http (default: grpc). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.protocol\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_INSECURE\fR
Disable TLS for the OTLP exporter (plaintext local\-collector setups) (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.insecure\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_SERVICE_NAME\fR
Value of the resource attribute service.name on emitted spans/metrics (default: magus). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.service_name\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_TELEMETRY_SAMPLE_RATIO\fR
Head\-based trace sampling ratio in [0,1] (default: 1.0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBtelemetry.sample_ratio\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_ENABLED\fR
When false, no command hands itself to a running `magus server`; each invocation runs self\-contained (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_ADDRESS\fR
Socket `magus server` listens on, as a unix:// URL; empty is server.sock in the runtime directory. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.address\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_IDLE_TTL\fR
Idle workspace eviction TTL for the multi\-workspace server; e.g. "6h", "30m" (default: 6h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.idle_ttl\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_WORKSPACES\fR
Colon\-separated list of workspace roots the server will serve; non\-empty list triggers eager union of sandbox policies and rejection of out\-of\-list workspaces (MGS2010). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.workspaces\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_ROTATE_ACTIVITIES\fR
How often the server checks whether the activity trail is due for a trim (default: 1h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.rotate_activities\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_ROTATE_LOGS\fR
How often the server checks the run\-log journals, and the age past which it trims them (default: 168h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.rotate_logs\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_PRUNE_PRESERVED\fR
How often the server checks for expired `vcs checkpoint \-\-preserve` captures (default: 24h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.prune_preserved\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_SYNC_GRAPH\fR
How often the server reconciles the knowledge graph, a safety net behind the VCS refresh hook (default: 6h). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.sync_graph\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SERVER_MAINTENANCE_CHECK_REVIEW\fR
How often the server checks for a merge or a new remark on a review this tree took part in (default: 15m). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBserver.maintenance.check_review\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_ENABLED\fR
When 0 or false, refuse to start the MCP server (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmcp.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_ADDRESS\fR
host:port for the MCP Streamable HTTP server `magus server` starts (default: 127.0.0.1:7391). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmcp.address\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_INSECURE_BIND\fR
Permit a non\-loopback mcp.address, which serves bearer tokens over plaintext HTTP; without it such an address is an error (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBmcp.insecure_bind\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CONSOLE_ENABLED\fR
When false, the MCP HTTP server does not mount the console's read\-only API and job service (default: true when MCP is up). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBconsole.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_HINTS_ENABLED\fR
When false, suppress all hint messages printed to stderr (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBhints.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_DIFF_TUI\fR
When false, `magus diff` prints its report instead of opening the interactive viewer (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBdiff.tui\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_MAX_DEPTH\fR
How many levels below its root job a `magus job fork` may land; 0 means unlimited (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.max_depth\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_MAX_LIVE\fR
How many live jobs one root's tree may hold at once, the new one included; 0 means unlimited (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.max_live\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT\fR
Timeout for a fork that names no \-\-timeout; 0 means no bound (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.default_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_JOBS_STALE_AFTER\fR
Flag a live job nobody updated for this long in `magus ls jobs` and `magus doctor`; 0 never flags (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBjobs.stale_after\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SECRET_INTERACTIVE_TIMEOUT\fR
Bound on a secret\-provider read when stdin is a terminal (default: 60s). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBsecret.interactive_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SECRET_UNATTENDED_TIMEOUT\fR
Bound on a secret\-provider read with no terminal to prompt on (default: 10s). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBsecret.unattended_timeout\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_WORKSPACES\fR
Comma\-separated extra workspace roots a \-\-global knowledge\-graph query unions in. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.workspaces\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_PUBLISHED_REF\fR
OCI artifact a published knowledge graph is read from, as <registry>/<repository>:<tag>. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.published_ref\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_MAX_SIZE_MB\fR
Soft cap on the knowledge shard store in MB; least\-recently\-used shards are evicted past it. 0 means unlimited (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.max_size_mb\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_VCS_ENABLED\fR
Fold VCS history (last commit, commit count) onto file nodes as the @vcs shard (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.vcs.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_VCS_MAX_COMMITS\fR
Bound the history walk to the most recent N commits; 0 uses a built\-in default (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.vcs.max_commits\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_VCS_AUTHORSHIP\fR
Include author nodes and authored edges in the @vcs shard; false keeps only the per\-file attributes (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.vcs.authorship\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_SYMBOL_INDEXING_DISABLED\fR
When true, the server never re\-runs a project's scip op on its own (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.symbol_indexing.disabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_SYMBOL_INDEXING_QUIET_SECONDS\fR
Seconds a project's sources must be quiet before the server re\-indexes it; 0 uses a built\-in default (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.symbol_indexing.quiet_seconds\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_SYMBOL_INDEXING_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS\fR
Minimum seconds between re\-index runs for one project; 0 uses a built\-in default (default: 0). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.symbol_indexing.min_interval_seconds\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_SESSIONS_DISABLED\fR
When true, `graph build` runs no agent\-session adapter (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.sessions.disabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_NOTES_SHARED\fR
Workspace\-relative directory of the team's committed notes. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.notes.shared\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_NOTES_PRIVATE\fR
A second notes directory, yours rather than the team's, anywhere on disk. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.notes.private\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_MIN_CALLEES\fR
Fewest callees a function needs before the duplication lens compares it (default: 3). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.min_callees\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_MIN_SHARED\fR
Fewest shared callees a pair needs to be reported as duplicates (default: 4). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.min_shared\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_MIN_SCORE\fR
Lowest similarity score in [0,1] the duplication lens reports (default: 0.7). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.min_score\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_MIN_SPAN_RATIO\fR
Lowest ratio in [0,1] of the shorter function's span to the longer one's (default: 0.5). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.min_span_ratio\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_KNOWLEDGE_DUPLICATION_INCLUDE_TESTS\fR
When true, the duplication lens also compares test functions (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBknowledge.duplication.include_tests\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_ENABLED\fR
Master switch for volatility detection and auto\-retry; false disables all retry logic (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_BOOTSTRAP_SAMPLES\fR
Number of outcomes below which all failures are retried once (bootstrap phase) (default: 20). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.bootstrap_samples\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_MIN_SAMPLES\fR
Minimum outcomes required before Wilson\-score volatility rate gates retry decisions (default: 20). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.min_samples\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_THRESHOLD\fR
Wilson lower\-bound volatility rate above which a project+target is considered volatile (default: 0.05). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.threshold\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_VOLATILITY_ANNOTATE_GHA\fR
When true, emit ::warning annotations and volatility summary to $GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY (default: true). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBvolatility.annotate_gha\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_REPORT_FILTER\fR
Comma\-separated +type/\-type terms restricting JSONL event emission (e.g. \-graph.build,\-graph.query). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBreport.filter\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SANDBOX_ENABLED\fR
When 1 or true, confine every subprocess and in\-process spell to the workspace + a curated allowlist, scrub the child\-process env to a minimum allowlist, and refuse paths outside it. See magus.yaml sandbox.allow and sandbox.env.passthrough for extension (default: false). Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBsandbox.enabled\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SANDBOX_ENV_PASSTHROUGH\fR
Comma\-separated names or globs (e.g. MISE_*) added to the sandbox's child\-process env allowlist. Equivalent magus.yaml key: \fBsandbox.env.passthrough\fR.
.TP
\fBMAGUS_UPDATE_URL\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: override the release index URL for `magus self update`; set to a self\-hosted copy of index.json to use a private update channel (default: https://eli.gladman.cc/magus/public/release/index.json)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_NO_BOOTSTRAP_EXEC\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: when 1, true or yes, disable the pre\-workspace\-load check that replaces this process with a workspace\-local ./magus found by walking up from the working directory (or \-\-root); set it to force the binary actually invoked to run instead, e.g. while debugging that binary itself (default: false)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_REGISTRY_URL\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: override the built\-in registry source's URL with a mirror of its signed index (default: https://eli.gladman.cc/magus/public/registry/index.json)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_OFFLINE\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: when set to anything but 0 or false, a registry or remote\-spell fetch fails with a named error instead of sending a request (default: false)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_DIFFTOOL\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: the command, taking two paths, that `\-\-then file <path> diff` compares a cached artifact with (default: $DIFFTOOL, then git diff \-\-no\-index)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LOG_VIEWER_URL\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: base URL of the log viewer page a live run opens, for a self\-hosted mirror (default: the hosted log viewer)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_CONSOLE_DIR\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: directory of the built console the LAN share serves (default: <root>/console/gen)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_PPROF\fR
Env\-only, no magus.yaml equivalent: write Go profiles for one invocation, as kind:path pairs (cpu, mem, trace), comma separated
.TP
\fBMAGUS_MCP_TOKEN\fR
Env\-only: the secret reference shipped harness spells name for the MCP bearer token; the environment secret provider reads it from this variable
.TP
\fBMAGUS_S3_BUCKET\fR
Env\-only: the bucket the aws/s3\-cache spell stores remote\-cache artifacts in
.TP
\fBMAGUS_S3_ENDPOINT\fR
Env\-only: the S3\-compatible endpoint the aws/s3\-cache spell talks to (default: https://s3.<region>.amazonaws.com)
.TP
\fBMAGUS_LEVEL\fR
Set by magus for the processes it spawns: the magus recursion depth, like make's MAKELEVEL; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_INVOCATION_ANCESTORS\fR
Set by magus for the processes it spawns: the comma\-separated invocations a nested magus runs underneath; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_BOOTSTRAP_EXEC_DONE\fR
Set by magus when it replaces itself with a workspace\-local ./magus, so the replacement never hops again; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_SYMBOL_INDEX\fR
Set by magus for a spell's scip op: the path the indexer writes its SCIP index to; never set it by hand
.TP
\fBMAGUS_INTERNAL_ADVICE_MODE\fR
Set by `magus diff` for the advice script it runs; the two halves of one feature, not a setting, and either may be renamed without notice
.TP
\fBMAGUS_INTERNAL_ADVICE_BASE_BRANCH\fR
Set by `magus diff` alongside MAGUS_INTERNAL_ADVICE_MODE; not a setting
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fBmagus.yaml\fR, \fB.magus.yaml\fR
Configuration file. Searched in CWD, workspace root, and
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/magus/ in ascending priority order. Both plain and
dot\-prefixed names are accepted; having both in the same directory is an error.
.TP
\fB.magus\-cache/\fR
Content\-addressed build cache in the workspace root. Override with
MAGUS_CACHE_DIR.
